WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.715 --> 00:00:13.355
met Jason and Bobby in the hallway after school.

2
00:00:13.375 --> 00:00:16.376
"I got the invitation to your party!"

3
00:00:16.717 --> 00:00:17.497
Jason said.

4
00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:21.898
"Yeah, cool invitation," Bobby said.

5
00:00:21.918 --> 00:00:24.239
"I liked the sharks."

6
00:00:25.879 --> 00:00:27.900
Ethan's birthday party was this Sunday.

7
00:00:28.916 --> 00:00:32.059
He and his mom had made invitations that looked like the ocean.

8
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.742
They had put little blue sharks on them.

9
00:00:36.742 --> 00:00:39.204
They had even glued real sand on the cards.

10
00:00:40.285 --> 00:00:45.149
"I'm coming to your birthday party, Ethan!"

11
00:00:45.529 --> 00:00:46.310
Izzie shouted.

12
00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:47.971
"Me too!"

13
00:00:48.412 --> 00:00:49.032
Nina said.

14
00:00:50.173 --> 00:00:51.794
Miss Shelly was setting up the table.

15
00:00:52.775 --> 00:00:55.077
Ethan felt bad for not inviting Miss Shelly.

16
00:00:56.038 --> 00:00:58.520
But no one invited teachers to birthday parties.

17
00:01:00.512 --> 00:01:04.794
"Today we're making a tasty birthday snack," Miss Shelly said.

18
00:01:04.814 --> 00:01:07.896
"We're making vanilla cupcakes!"

19
00:01:08.757 --> 00:01:12.619
"Yum! I've never made cupcakes," Izzie said.

20
00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.740
"Put on your aprons.

21
00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.181
Things might get messy!"

22
00:01:17.541 --> 00:01:18.462
Miss Shelly said.

23
00:01:24.045 --> 00:01:25.906
going to use the hand mixer."

24
00:01:25.926 --> 00:01:29.908
"Ooh, that looks fancy," Nina said.

25
00:01:31.048 --> 00:01:33.150
"Like something a real chef has!

26
00:01:34.311 --> 00:01:35.312
How do you use it?"

27
00:01:35.332 --> 00:01:37.374
"It's easy.

28
00:01:38.194 --> 00:01:39.976
We put the ingredients in a bowl.

29
00:01:40.957 --> 00:01:43.859
Then we turn on the mixer," Miss Shelly explained.

30
00:01:43.879 --> 00:01:45.961
"What goes in first?"

31
00:01:46.402 --> 00:01:47.342
Jason asked.

32
00:01:47.362 --> 00:01:54.188
"Flour, sugar, baking powder, and salt," Ethan read.

33
00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.992
Nina and Izzie measured the flour and sugar.

34
00:02:00.096 --> 00:02:02.237
Jason measured the baking powder and salt.

35
00:02:02.257 --> 00:02:04.278
"Here's a whisk!"

36
00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:05.359
Bobby said.

37
00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:08.921
Ethan used the whisk to mix the dry ingredients.

38
00:02:08.941 --> 00:02:13.103
"I'll preheat the toaster oven," Nina said.

39
00:02:13.123 --> 00:02:16.205
"Now we need the wet ingredients.

40
00:02:17.385 --> 00:02:22.148
Butter, egg, egg yolks, vanilla, and sour cream," Jason read.

41
00:02:22.168 --> 00:02:25.710
"How do we get just egg yolks?"

42
00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:29.352
"Crack them into a bowl," Miss Shelly said.

43
00:02:30.896 --> 00:02:34.560
"And scoop up the yolk with a fork," Miss Shelly went on.

44
00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:37.944
Jason cracked two eggs into a bowl.

45
00:02:39.906 --> 00:02:41.528
Next he separated the yolks.

46
00:02:46.974 --> 00:02:47.774
wasn't so hard!"

47
00:02:49.997 --> 00:02:52.660
The kids added the other wet ingredients to the bowl.

48
00:03:00.416 --> 00:03:03.378
Nina poured the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients.

49
00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.681
They all took turns using the mixer.

50
00:03:12.185 --> 00:03:13.406
made cupcakes!"

51
00:03:14.407 --> 00:03:15.127
cried Nina.

52
00:03:15.147 --> 00:03:16.889
"Not yet!

53
00:03:17.609 --> 00:03:19.831
They're not baked," Miss Shelly said.

54
00:03:20.812 --> 00:03:22.913
The kids filled the baking cups with batter.

55
00:03:24.054 --> 00:03:25.916
They put the tray in the toaster oven.

56
00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:35.087
"You can't put icing on cupcakes until they cool," Miss Shelly said.

57
00:03:35.107 --> 00:03:38.150
"But I baked some cupcakes last night."

58
00:03:39.831 --> 00:03:42.013
She pulled out cupcakes from under the table.

59
00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:44.836
"We'll decorate these today."

60
00:03:44.856 --> 00:03:47.137
"Oh, those look good!"

61
00:03:47.558 --> 00:03:48.258
Ethan said.

62
00:03:48.278 --> 00:03:53.723
"Your mom showed me your party invitations," Miss Shelly said.

63
00:03:53.743 --> 00:03:55.224
"She did?"

64
00:03:55.645 --> 00:03:57.386
Ethan asked, surprised.

65
00:03:58.507 --> 00:03:59.468
"They were great!"

66
00:04:00.532 --> 00:04:01.653
Miss Shelly smiled.

67
00:04:02.653 --> 00:04:03.834
Ethan was relieved.

68
00:04:04.714 --> 00:04:06.716
She wasn't upset that she wasn't invited!

69
00:04:06.736 --> 00:04:11.198
"They gave me an idea," Miss Shelly continued.

70
00:04:13.459 --> 00:04:16.141
"Here is white icing and blue food coloring.

71
00:04:17.362 --> 00:04:19.923
We'll dye the icing so it looks like waves."

72
00:04:21.224 --> 00:04:22.345
She held up a bowl.

73
00:04:22.365 --> 00:04:24.986
"These are crushed graham crackers.

74
00:04:26.047 --> 00:04:26.967
They look like sand!"

75
00:04:29.708 --> 00:04:32.151
"And there are even little surfboards!"

76
00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:33.253
Bobby said.

77
00:04:34.895 --> 00:04:36.977
Ethan spread blue icing on his cupcake.

78
00:04:38.079 --> 00:04:40.401
He dipped half the cupcake in the graham crackers.

79
00:04:41.503 --> 00:04:44.366
Then he stuck a surfboard in the blue, sugary waves.

80
00:04:46.389 --> 00:04:48.732
It was one cool birthday cupcake!
